<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sievershausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1553">1553</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-margrave-war">Second Margrave War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sievershausen was fought on 9 July 1553 near Lehrte in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a> between Elector Maurice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and Margrave Albert <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcibiades">Alcibiades</a> of Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a>, whose plundering campaigns threatened the peace of the Empire. Maurice won, but he was mortally wounded and died two days later. It was one of the bloodiest battles fought in sixteenth-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sievershausen.jpg" alt="Battle of Sievershausen" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sievershausen_Schlacht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
